  "_comment": "Set your tickers in 'watchlist'. A rule whose tickers are [\"@watchlist\"] uses that list. AN EMPTY WATCHLIST MEANS EVERY TICKER, NOT NONE - so out of the box this alerts on any emiten a rule accepts. Narrow it in Options, or here.",
  "_roundup_note": "global_exclude carries ROUNDUP_MARKERS incl. foreign-flow phrases. max_tickers=2 drops any headline naming 3+ companies - measured on 69 real alerts 2026-09-09, that is the shape of a movers list. Two tickers is legitimate ('MERGER ADHI KARYA DAN PTPP').",
  "_sources_note": "enabled/disabled from measured f-tick% on Mon 2026-09-07 18:26 WIB, after a full trading day. Morning readings were misleading: wartaekonomi and idxchannel both scored 0% pre-open and 30-35% post-close. Re-measure with 'python jci.py --density' before changing this.",
  "_categories_note": "expanded from 162 real alerts on 2026-09-09 (86 of them uncategorised). ownership/structure/rating_credit/csr are new; single-word event terms carry a trailing * because Indonesian suffixes defeat exact matching ('Simak Prospeknya' never matched 'prospek'). Put 'csr' in a rule's exclude list to drop corporate PR - the banks publish a lot of it. Re-validate any change with: python jci.py --report --recategorize",
  "corner": "bottom right"
